Fix two issues in the ZIP codes page of the Zip Code Checker app at /Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Shopify App/Zip-Code:

## Step 1: Read the file completely first
Read `app/routes/app.zip-codes.tsx` in full. Pay close attention to:
1. The export CSV logic (search for "export" — find the action handler and the UI button/handler)
2. The import modal UI (search for "import" — find the modal and the dropzone/upload area)

---

## Bug Fix 1: Export CSV downloads multiple times

The export button is triggering multiple downloads. This is almost certainly caused by a `useEffect` or `fetcher.data` watcher that fires multiple times.

**Find the pattern:** Look for something like:
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (actionData?.csv || fetcher.data?.csv) {
    // trigger download
  }
}, [actionData, fetcher.data]);
```

The problem is likely that `actionData` persists across renders and triggers the download again on re-renders.

**Fix:** Add a ref to track whether a download has already been triggered for the current response:

```typescript
const downloadedRef = useRef<string | null>(null);

useEffect(() => {
  const csvData = fetcher.data?.csv ?? actionData?.csv;
  if (csvData && downloadedRef.current !== csvData) {
    downloadedRef.current = csvData;
    const blob = new Blob([csvData], { type: "text/csv" });
    const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
    const a = document.createElement("a");
    a.href = url;
    a.download = "zip-codes.csv";
    document.body.appendChild(a);
    a.click();
    document.body.removeChild(a);
    URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
  }
}, [fetcher.data, actionData]);
```

Replace whatever the current export download logic looks like with this ref-guarded version. Import `useRef` if not already imported.

Alternatively, if the export works by the action returning CSV data and a button click causing a form submit — check if there are multiple fetcher submissions happening. The button might be inside a `<Form>` that also submits on Enter, causing double submission.

Read the actual code and apply the correct targeted fix based on what you find.

---

## Feature: Add "Download Sample CSV" button inside the import modal

Find the import modal (Modal component for CSV import). Inside the modal, find the DropZone or file upload area. 

**Add a sample CSV download link ABOVE the dropzone**, inside a `<BlockStack gap="300">`:

```tsx
<InlineStack align="end">
  <Button
    variant="plain"
    icon={ExportIcon}
    onClick={() => {
      const sample = `Zip Code,Zone,Status,Message,ETA
10001,Manhattan,allowed,We deliver to your area!,2-3 business days
10002,Manhattan,allowed,Fast delivery available,1-2 business days
90210,Beverly Hills,blocked,Sorry we don't deliver here yet,
`;
      const blob = new Blob([sample], { type: "text/csv" });
      const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      const a = document.createElement("a");
      a.href = url;
      a.download = "sample-zip-codes.csv";
      document.body.appendChild(a);
      a.click();
      document.body.removeChild(a);
      URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
    }}
  >
    Download Sample CSV
  </Button>
</InlineStack>
```

Place this BEFORE the DropZone in the import modal section. Import `ExportIcon` from `@shopify/polaris-icons` if not already imported.

